== Match report ==

=== Jarin 1–0 Nusaraya ===
[[Jarin national football team|Jarin]] needed just one goal to see off [[Nusaraya national football team|Nusaraya]] in [[Castramara]], with Petros Shimora scoring the match's only goal in the 25th minute. Nusaraya pressed late, but Jarin's structure held and the Mesogean side opened their campaign with a narrow victory.

=== Asikyira 3–5 United Midlands ===
[[United Midlands national football team|United Midlands]] produced the standout performance of the day, defeating [[Asikyira national football team|Asikyira]] in a wildly open match in [[Sanropura]]. Oliver Hartley struck early, and although Asikyira answered through Amadou Baal, the Lurandians kept extending their lead through Samuel Wren, Ethan Mercer and Thomas Vale. Asikyira twice hauled themselves back into the contest through Boubacar Sarr and Idrissa Koné, but Callum Ashby sealed the away win late on.

=== Burawa 4–3 Daras ===
[[Burawa national football team|Burawa]] and [[Daras national football team|Daras]] produced the wildest finish of the day in [[San Chorche]]. Burawa went two up through Petre Xirsi and Qaasim Dhaxol, only for Daras to roar back with late goals from Chen Zihang and Wang Yuchen. The game then exploded in stoppage time, as Yaxye Cumar and Xirsi Shire restored Burawa's lead before Li Haoran pulled one back again in the 93rd minute.

=== Varkana 2–0 Pangkajene ===
[[Varkana national football team|Varkana]] made a fast start in [[Telukuba]], with Hugo Loria scoring inside the opening minute to settle the match early. [[Pangkajene national football team|Pangkajene]] stayed in the contest for long spells, but Luka Paliashvili's late strike made sure of the result and gave Varkana a comfortable-looking win on the scoreline.

=== Orma 0–0 Sarta ===
[[Orma national football team|Orma]] and [[Sarta national football team|Sarta]] played out a cagey goalless draw in [[Pangkalsimpang]]. Both sides were organised and disciplined, but neither could find the decisive moment needed to break the deadlock.

=== Aetolia 1–1 Louyang ===
[[Louyang national football team|Louyang]] took an early lead in [[Valparaíso]] through Chen Minghao, but [[Aetolia national football team|Aetolia]] responded before the half-hour mark when Nikos Stavridis equalised. The rest of the match remained tight, with both sides settling for a point after a balanced encounter.

== Summary ==

The second matchday featured two tight one-goal wins, two draws, and two high-tempo thrillers. United Midlands' away win over Asikyira was the day's biggest upset, while Burawa's late escape against Daras provided the most dramatic finish.

